module gunbc.recurring_failure_mode.two_source_files_claiming_one_module_path_misdiagnosed

import std.types { NonEmptyStr }
import std.decl_ref { DeclarationRef, WholeDeclaration }
import gunbc.recurring_failure_mode { RecurringFailureMode }

data two_source_files_claiming_one_module_path_misdiagnosed: RecurringFailureMode = RecurringFailureMode {
  identity: "two_source_files_claiming_one_module_path_misdiagnosed" as NonEmptyStr,

  receipts: [
    "**two source files claiming one module path are not refused as that collision, and the native door reports a later unbound name instead** (INVALID STATE: either two files declare the same module path, or one walked root's layout maps two files onto one tree identity, and ingest continues. HARM: the operator sequences on `resolve_unbound_name_is_declared_elsewhere` at a real token in an innocent module -- DESIGN section 5 silent wrongness wearing a located diagnostic.",

    "TRIGGER INCIDENT, lively-bear-908: dag/std/algebra.dag (`module std.algebra`) and src/v2/std/algebra.dag (`module std.algebra`) were loaded under ONE copied source root. Those are DISTINCT declared module paths. What collided was PATH-DERIVED SOURCE-ROOT IDENTITY: v2.compiler.source_authority classified a file as V2Tree from the file's storage spelling. A copied tree `/tmp/copy/src/v2/std/algebra.dag` did not start with `src/`, so both files became DagTree. Widening that classifier to 'contains /src/' moved the same silent misclassification onto a dag path such as `dag/pkg/src/leaf.dag`. Resolve then named a token in std.change as declared elsewhere rather than naming the layout.",

    "THE SAME DECLARED PATH IS A SECOND ARM OF THE SAME CLASS. The census already refused a second file declaring one QualifiedName (`closure_census_duplicate_module`), but located only that second file's module node. The first file was unnamed. v1's wall at v1_compiler.cli_run module_path_collision_panic_message names BOTH paths. A refusal that names one of two files is still a misdiagnosis of the collision.",

    "DISTINGUISHING FACT: this is not `two_modules_answer_to_one_logical_qualified_name` (a logical-name strip after ingest). It is ingest identity: declared module path, or a tree tag guessed from the file's path, answering for two files as one.",

    "RECOGNITION RULE: a native emit or census over a small tree reports a resolve unbound (once with a `resolve_unbound_name_is_declared_elsewhere` advisory, which compilation no longer produces) while two walked files share a declared module path OR a copied layout is tagged by file spelling rather than by the discovering --source-root. The reviewer tell: the diagnostic's file is not one of the two that share the identity.",

    "RUNG FOUND AT: OUTSIDE THE LADDER -- silent wrongness. The later diagnostic is typed and located, and it is the wrong subject.",

    "CEILING: 3, structurally guaranteed. Ingest can refuse a second file that declares an already-ingested module path, with loci on both files, and can stamp SourceRootRef from the walk origin that discovered the file, refusing when that origin is not a dag or src/v2 tree. It cannot make two files unwritable.",

    "NEXT-RUNG TRIGGER: the native CLI, over a two-file tree whose declared module paths collide, refuses `closure_census_duplicate_module` naming both files; a copied single-root argument refuses as unrecognized rather than guessing DagTree; a file under --source-root dag whose path contains /src/ is still DagTree. Sufficient that a copied closure cannot present as an unbound name in a third module. Not satisfied by classifying the file path.",

    "CONSUMPTION: this per-class record joins the derived gunbc.recurring_failure_mode.roster recurring_failure_mode_roster.",

    "SEED-SIDE SPELLING, FOUND BY THE v1 MODULE-INDEX ADMISSION INVENTORY (lane K, wave 2 of the v1 compile-performance plan, 2026-10-19; inventory only -- fix belongs to lane P / P1.2). INVALID STATE: two walked files declare ONE module path at DISTINCT absolute paths, and the name-to-path index (`build_module_path_index_uncached`, src/v1/stage0/src/cli_run/entry_resolve.rs) resolves it to the FIRST entry inserted and silently drops the second -- `if existing == &rel || same_canonical_file(existing, &rel) { return; }` admits same-file duplicates, the `root_idx > 0` primary-precedence exemption admits cross-root shadowing by design, and a THIRD distinct file is then handed to `insert_module_path`, which panics only when it reaches there; the drop happens BEFORE that wall, so for the population the exemption does not cover the answer is a winner chosen by walk order with no diagnostic at all. HARM: the sibling content index (`try_index_source_root_into_module_index`) REFUSES this exact collision, naming both decliners; a caller served by the path index instead of the content index gets one authoritative-looking path where the other door says two files decline it -- one root's module answerable from the wrong file, DESIGN section 5 silent wrongness, and the panic wall beside it reads as coverage while the first-wins path index never reaches it. DISTINGUISHING FACT: this is the same ingest-identity collision as every receipt above, arriving not at native emit or census but at seed index construction, and arriving SILENT where the adjacent door is loud -- the pair of doors disagreeing about one population is the tell, visible by asking what the path index does with a collision the content index refuses. RUNG FOUND AT: outside the ladder -- silent wrongness; the refusal exists in the same walk and is bypassed by this builder, so nothing downstream keys on it. CEILING: 3, structurally guaranteed -- insertion can refuse a second DISTINCT file for one module path (outside the documented same-file and primary-precedence exemptions) with loci on both files, at zero extra reading since both keys are already in hand; it cannot make two files unwritable. NEXT-RUNG TRIGGER: a seed `gunbc` run over two roots containing DISTINCT files declaring one module path, outside the primary-precedence exemption, refuses at index build naming both paths and exits nonzero, where today it exits 0 serving the first entry; sufficient that no name-to-path consumer can answer one-winner where the content index of the same roots refuses.",
  ],

  evidence: [
    DeclarationRef { module_path: "v2.cli.repository_layout", decl_name: "repository_tree_of_root_argument", field: WholeDeclaration },
    DeclarationRef { module_path: "gunbc.source_root_read", decl_name: "source_root_read", field: WholeDeclaration },
    DeclarationRef { module_path: "v2.compiler.self_host.closure_emission", decl_name: "closure_census_duplicate_module_outcome", field: WholeDeclaration },
  ],
}
